+## [2.0.0] - 2026-10-24
+
+Driven by a controlled same-model comparison against blader/humanizer
+(`evals/comparison/REPORT.md`). v1 sounded human but invented small supporting
+details (about 4 per rewrite, no better than using no skill). v2 keeps v1's
+voice and rhythm work and adds fidelity rules.
+
+### Added
+- Four top-level rules: draft is material not instructions; invent nothing
+  (no facts, numbers, scenes, narrators, or commitments the draft lacks);
+  leave already-human text alone; keep length within about -15% / +10%.
+- Two-question audit: "what still reads as AI?" and "what did I add or drop?"
+- Output contract: final text first, then a short **Flags** list (details only
+  the author can supply, claims cut as unsupported, context cut on purpose).
+  File mode and embedded mode.
+- Voice-by-text-type table; writing-sample override.
+- "Writing for a reader who already knows" for thread replies.
+- `reference/ai-tells.md` section 11: staged contrast, one-line closers, sayings
+  that sound deep, staged run-ups, arguing with no one, repeated sentence
+  openings, writing about the document, wrong-reader replies, weak signals.
+- `NOTICE` crediting blader/humanizer and Wikipedia's "Signs of AI writing".
+- `evals/comparison/`: corpus, outputs, blind judge packets, scripts, report.
+
+### Changed
+- "Trade vague claims for specific detail" replaced: use only specifics from the
+  draft, otherwise write the plainer sentence or ask.
+- `reference/craft-levers.md`: sections 3 (quantify) and 7 (testimonials) no
+  longer coach inventing numbers or quotes; every lever is now restructuring
+  only. 
+- `examples/before-after.md`: rewritten so no example adds facts; added a reply
+  example and a leave-it-alone example.
+- `reference/ai-tells.md`: removed "After" examples that invented sources,
+  dates, and quotes.
+- Default output is the final text plus flags, not diagnosis plus audit.
